    "title": "Woman charged with giving THC candy to 4 young kids at Wheeling park fails to appear in court - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By ABC7 Chicago Digital Team ,\n3 hours ago\nAn arrest warrant has been issued for a woman who is facing charges for allegedly giving THC-infused chocolates to children at a north suburban park, authorities said.\nWheeling police officers initially took 48-year-old Dagmara J. Rouse into custody in May . She is now wanted for missing two court dates, officials said.\nABC7 Chicago is now streaming 24/7. Click here to watch Police are now seeking to arrest Rouse after she failed to appear in court Wednesday after also skipping her first court date July 31, officials said.\nThe Robbins woman allegedly gave four children, two 9-year-olds, a 6-year-old and a 2-year-old, the candy at Pleasant Run/Four Acres Park earlier this year .\nAll four kids became \"fatigued and lethargic\" after eating the candy, police said. They were taken to a local hospital for evaluation, and at least one of them tested positive for THC, a psychoactive compound found in cannabis.\nOfficers found a product labeled \"MOJO THC MILK CHOCOLATE\" while searching the park.\nRouse is facing four counts of Delivery of Cannabis to a Minor, four counts of Contributing to the Delinquency of a Minor and four counts of Endangering the Life or Health of a Child.\nWheeling police asked anyone with information to contact them.\n4",
